<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nsundi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nsundi was a province of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kongo">Kingdom of Kongo</a>, located in the north of the kingdom in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/democratic-republic-of-the-congo">Democratic Republic of the Congo</a>. By the late fifteenth century it was one of the provinces, alongside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soyo">Soyo</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mbata">Mbata</a>, under the authority of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manikongo">manikongo</a>. It formed part of the territorial core of the Kongo Empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nsundi.jpg" alt="Nsundi" width="320" height="280" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: HetmanTheResearcher · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:West_Central_Africa_1350CE.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
